import KaburioPolicyLayout from "../../../../layouts/KaburioPolicyLayout.astro";
---

<KaburioPolicyLayout lang="en">
  <p>This policy applies to the ad-free Android build (versionCode 3 and later). If you use an earlier build with ads, see the <a href="/kaburio/privacy/legacy-ads/en/">legacy advertising policy</a>.</p>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-1">
    <h2 id="section-1">1. Operator and app</h2>
    <p>TATTO LAB (the “Operator”) provides KABURIO for Android, package name com.tattolab.kaburio. This policy explains how information is handled in the app.</p>
    <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:tattoqq9@gmail.com">tattoqq9@gmail.com</a></p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-2">
    <h2 id="section-2">2. Photos, videos, audio, and head information</h2>
    <p>The app uses the camera and photos, videos, and your own image or 3D materials you select to capture, edit, add image or 3D stickers, and save creations. It also uses the microphone if you allow recording with audio.</p>
    <p>Photo and video processing and estimation of head position and orientation run on your device. The app does not send these photos, videos, audio, head positions, or angles to the Operator’s or advertising providers’ servers.</p>
    <p>When you choose to share a creation, the app passes it to the app you select. The receiving service’s privacy policy applies to its handling of that content.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-3">
    <h2 id="section-3">3. Information stored on your device</h2>
    <p>The app stores settings, favorites, imported materials, editing drafts, information for restoring unfinished edits, face coverage review records and images.</p>
    <p>Copies of photos, materials, person positions, and adjustments needed for drafts or edit recovery may be stored in the app’s private storage. These copies stay on your device.</p>
    <p>Rendered preview images are stored temporarily in the app’s private cache. Older temporary files are cleaned up during later review operations and can also be removed by clearing the app cache in Android settings.</p>
    <p>Exported creations are saved to your device’s media storage or a destination you choose.</p>
    <p>You can remove app information using available material deletion actions, by clearing app data in Android settings, or by uninstalling the app. Exported, copied, or shared files remain separately and must be deleted from their destinations when needed.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-4">
    <h2 id="section-4">4. Advertising, purchases, and external transfers</h2>
    <p>All current features are free, including importing and using your own image and 3D materials. This build has no ads, in-app purchases, advertising SDK, advertising consent SDK, or SDK that automatically sends usage analytics or crash reports. It does not ask for an age range for advertising.</p>
    <p>Editing and estimation run on your device. The app does not collect or send IP addresses, approximate location, advertising IDs, app set IDs, interactions, or diagnostics for advertising or analytics.</p>
    <p>If you choose to share a creation, read the privacy policy, or contact support by email, the app opens another app or browser. The receiving app, email service, and website handle information under their own policies. Processing by the operating system or a file provider is separate from the app’s local processing.</p>
    <p>After updating from a build with ads, the app cleans up locally stored advertising age ranges, ad frequency state, and old consent signals when it opens. This cleanup does not remove photos, videos, your materials, drafts, or editing settings. It cannot erase information already sent by an older SDK; see the providers’ controls linked in the legacy advertising policy for that information.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-5">
    <h2 id="section-5">5. Permissions and user actions</h2>
    <p>You can change camera and microphone permissions in Android settings.</p>
    <p>The app uses photos, videos, and PNG materials you choose. You can find this policy and contact details under “Privacy and support” in the app.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-6">
    <h2 id="section-6">6. Retention and deletion requests</h2>
    <p>The Operator does not run servers that store the app’s photos, videos, audio, or head information. See section 3 for deleting information on your device.</p>
    <p>If you contact support by email, your email address and message are used to respond and resolve the issue. This information is kept for as long as needed for that purpose and removed when no longer necessary. Contact the email address above for deletion inquiries.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-7">
    <h2 id="section-7">7. Age group</h2>
    <p>The app is intended for users aged 13 and over and is not directed at children under 13. Minors should consult a parent or guardian where appropriate.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="section-8">
    <h2 id="section-8">8. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated as the app or its information handling changes. Updates will be posted on this page. Significant changes may also be announced in the app or through other appropriate means.</p>
  </section>
</KaburioPolicyLayout>
